				\begin{document}$${b}_{1}$$\end{document}b1), concatenated them into a single vector, and used this vector as input for the traditional ML methods. Thus, our original model was first trained and tested in a five-fold cross validation process, and the traditional ML models were trained and tested on the same cross-fold split afterwards. The encoder’s weights were frozen during this process.Fig. 6
The pipeline of the traditional ML methods. The encoded features of our original deep learning model are extracted and concatenated into one feature vector. All four methods (SVM, logistic regression, random forest, and XGBoost) take this feature vector as input and output the pCR prediction

Tables 2A and B summarize the results of the performance metric to predict pCR. AUC for the clinical data only, image data only, and attention-fused clinical + imaging data were, respectively, 0.66 ± 0.08, 0.68 ± 0.03, and 0.73 ± 0.04, for the internal validation dataset (I-SPY 2), and 0.71 ± 0.03, 0.70 ± 0.04, and 0.71 ± 0.02 for the external validation dataset (I-SPY 1). The combined clinical + imaging model performed better than either alone in both internal and external validation datasets.Table 2
